If a patient receives an opioid-therapy for an acute-pain during at least 1 month then every clinician should address a potentially-reversible-chronic-pain-cause and should reassess the opioid-therapy and should prevent an unintentional-long-term-opioid-therapy.
If a patient receives an opioid-therapy for an acute-pain during at least 1 month and a clinician does not provably reassess the opioid-therapy then it is recommended that the clinician does not continue the opioid-therapy for the patient.
